<p></p>
<p></p>
<i>
<p></p>
According to the Call Reports, auto loans at banks have grown rapidly this year.
	 Questions 30-31 ask you to compare your bank&#8217;s current policies
	 on approving applications for auto loans that your bank characterizes as <b>subprime</b>

	 with the stance of those policies a year ago. 
	 Question 32 asks about how you expect lending policies for auto loans categorized 
	 by your bank as subprime to change at your institution over the next year. 
	 (Please consider only loans to individuals and households and report changes in enforcement of
	 existing policies as changes in policies)
        </i>
